= A Purge of the Corrupt

The Chancellery announces that the Republic will be cleaned up at last. Judicial officers arrive at the offices of senators accused of corruption, and the list is long. Most of the accused are guilty of something. All of them, as it happens, have spoken against the Chancellor's powers. Several of them signed the Caucus's petition, and several more quietly take their names off it.
